---
// Fig. for "Multivariate & Multilinear Polynomials": why a single random
// check catches a cheating prover — tying Schwartz–Zippel to a concrete
// soundness argument, with a cheat that happens to survive one bad-luck
// check before a second check catches it.
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 760 400" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
  <text x="380" y="26" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="16" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">one random check catches a cheater</text>

  <rect x="40" y="46" width="680" height="42" rx="10" fill="#111c2e" stroke="#3ab7ff" stroke-width="1.5" />
  <text x="380" y="72" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="13" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">Why does checking at one random point actually catch a lie?</text>

  <text x="380" y="122" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">CLAIM&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13" font-weight="700">prover says A(x) &#215; B(x) = C(x) for every x in F(13)</tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="154" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">CHECK&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#8fdcff" font-size="13" font-weight="700">verifier picks random r, tests A(r) &#215; B(r) =? C(r)</tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="186" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11" font-weight="700">WHY IT WORKS&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#e9eef5" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700">g(x) = A(x)B(x) &#8722; C(x) is nonzero, degree &#8804; 2 &#8594; at most 2 roots</tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="218" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11" font-weight="700">CHEAT EXAMPLE&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#e9eef5" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700">this false claim's g(x) happens to vanish at x = 1 and x = 7</tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="250" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">TRY r = 1&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#ff5c7a" font-size="13" font-weight="700">g(1) = 0 &#8594; check passes, cheater gets lucky &#10007;</tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="282" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">TRY r = 2&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="13" font-weight="700">g(2) = 5 &#8800; 0 &#8594; check fails, cheater is caught &#10003;</tspan>
  </text>

  <rect x="60" y="300" width="640" height="38" rx="10" fill="#0e1f16" stroke="#5ddc8a" stroke-width="1.8" />
  <text x="380" y="324" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="13" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">repeat 3 times: chance every check gets lucky &#8804; (2/13)<tspan dy="-5" font-size="65%">3</tspan><tspan dy="5"> &#8776; 0.4%</tspan></text>

  <line x1="40" y1="352" x2="720" y2="352" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />
  <text x="380" y="376" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="15" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">A FEW RANDOM CHECKS SHRINK THE CHEATING CHANCE FAST</text>
  <text x="380" y="394" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">In a huge field, one check is already enough.</text>
</svg>
